  "description": "When we launched the Synonym two years ago, many doubted its viability. Its ultra-slack head angle, massive reach, and steep seat tube were unprecedented in short travel bikes, especially for XC racing. However, the Synonym signaled a new era in bike design. Today, we see that progressive geometry is crucial even for XC. The Synonym rides like an enduro bike on descents, climbs efficiently, and speeds across flats. Our prototypes exceeded expectations on downhills and also excelled on climbs and flats. This is due to a better weight distribution and a lower cockpit position, which enhances both climbing and stability. The RC range, designed for XC racing and marathons, features a lightweight full carbon frame with flex stays, a flat bar, cross-country tires, and 100mm of travel front and rear, making it a versatile choice for serious riders.\nINTENDED USE CATEGORY 4: XC & TRAIL\nMAIN FEATURES:\n- Super lightweight carbon frame\n- Unique geometry, unprecedented in this category\n- 100mm front / 100mm rear wheel travel\n- Fox 32 Step Cast Factory fork\n- Fox DPS Factory shock\n- Dual remote for fork & shock\n- 12-speed SRAM X01 Eagle rear derailleur\n- Fox Transfer sl Factory dropper post\n- ultralight NS carbon flat handlebar\n- ultralight NS x Hunt Straight pull wheels\nRADICAL, UNPRECEDENTED GEOMETRY\nThe longest, slackest XC bike on the market! No other bike comes even close!!!\nFLEX STAYS\nFlex stays eliminate the need for a pivot in the rear triangle. less weight, more lateral stffness..\nFRAME DESIGN\nBeautiful lines by George Dabrowski. Designer of award winning Rondo bikes.",
